    <desc>Make the text of a terminal larger or smaller.</desc>
  </info>

  <title>Zoom in and zoom out</title>

<p>To make the text larger, press <keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>+</key></keyseq>, or press the menu
  button in the top-right corner of the window and click the
  <gui style="button">+</gui> button at the top of the menu.</p>

  <p>To make it smaller, press <keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>-</key></keyseq>, or click the
  <gui style="button">-</gui> button.</p>

  <p>The zoom level, such as <gui>120%</gui>, is shown between the two
  buttons. To return to the normal size, press <keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>0</key></keyseq>,
  or click the zoom level.</p>

  <p>Zooming changes the number of columns and rows that fit in the window;
  the window keeps its size.</p>

  <p>To change the font for good, see <link xref="app-fonts"/>.</p>

